From 0033f8dd69d6007c2c7832f428fd282c639f1a2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:35:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban edit: refuse to lower a card's priority
 without --reason

A chat ran `kanban edit <id> --priority 10` on a stale read and silently undid
another actor's raise to 150. The CLI now refuses a lowering with no --reason
(exit 1, naming the current value); with --reason the change applies and the
reason lands in the reprioritized event payload. The check runs inside
edit_task's write transaction (opt-in require_lower_reason), plus a pre-check
before operator fields commit so a refused edit applies nothing. Raising or
re-setting the same value is unchanged. Dashboard and REST callers of
edit_task are unchanged (they don't opt in).

edit_task moves to hermes_cli/kanban_db_edit.py (re-exported from kanban_db)
to keep kanban_db.py under its line cap.
